    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by three core high-ceiling plays. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.01) leads the charge against Quinn Mathews; despite the lefty matchup, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** retains immense value due to a favorable park factor and a premium spot in the two-hole. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) follow closely, both benefitting from soft matchups against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez and Framber Valdez, respectively. **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) is our premier utility play today, as his switch-hitting profile and elite park factors in his matchup against Luinder Avila drive his efficiency score well into the top tier. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (68.40) serves as our most reliable outfielder, leveraging a dynamic platoon advantage against Tyler Mahle to secure a strong 68.40 projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Andy Pages** (53.37) on the bench. He finished just outside the active cut, with the optimizer favoring the platoon depth of **Dominic Smith** (57.69) against the vulnerable Miles Mikolas. While **Andy Pages** brings high upside, his matchup against the tougher Payton Tolle suppressed his raw score just enough to keep him as a reserve. We are also monitoring several weather-related risks: the trio of **Drake Baldwin**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Nasim Nunez** are all tethered to the 37% rain risk in their respective games. While **Drake Baldwin** (69.59) remains a strong start due to his elite xwOBA metrics, managers should keep a close eye on the radar, as a postponement for these players would necessitate a rapid shuffle of our bench assets like **Gunnar Henderson** or **Coby Mayo**.\n\nRegarding our positional strategy, note that while **Gunnar Henderson** (53.01) and **Coby Mayo** (49.56) were deemed sub-optimal by the projection model, both are high-variance alternatives should late-breaking lineup news change the projected order for our starters. We are prioritizing the stolen base potential across our active roster, as our reliance on players like **Jacob Wilson** and **Cole Carrigg** is intended to insulate our scoring in that scarcity-driven category. Be advised that **Liam Hicks** (43.45) is currently operating near his floor, and if he is not confirmed at the top of the order, he becomes a prime candidate for a late-afternoon swap to maximize our daily efficiency caps.",
